itself reads its control files and GitHub executes workflow/action configuration; AGENTS/CLAUDE are agent instruction files, not an invented rules.json reader. Ordinary content extents and the catch-all source extent remain writable; do not reserve every classified path. No separate repository rules.json/artroom.json control reader was found in this trace. A final implementation head report must give this path/reader table and exact dynamic rules basis.\n\nSmallest coherent implementation sequence:\n1. Add a shared pure bounded application-publication policy module: canonical literal slash-terminated directory prefixes, a precise fixed-reserved predicate, declared-prefix membership, and current rules/authority/effective-link classification. Reuse the existing bounded extent grammar/matcher; no unbounded regex search, filesystem follow, public status endpoint or new general Git restriction. Application file publication only is gated; change-lane review, first-head creation, archive refs and receipts retain their separate contracts.\n2. Add an explicitly versioned signed semantic publication declaration (proposed shape publication:{prefixes:[...]}) and strict package/proof codec/packer. Keep old exact-key v1/v2 codecs, signatures, digest goldens and historical readers unchanged; absence means no publication authority. Next Lending declares shelf/; Grow declares no prefixes. Do not rewrite deployed signed bytes. Count/byte bounds must be recorded in the reviewed new schema; the earlier 16-prefix/256-byte design is a proposal, not a newly adopted quota here.\n3. Add only the new native Rules/Directory/Destination cohort identities needed to admit and carry the signed declaration. Bind release, definition and resulting full child reference through the actual install/creation proof, not application name or caller fields. Install checks the declaration against current protected policy before creating the application. New Destination judgment rechecks the declared prefix and current protected paths, records precise reserved/undeclared reasons, and refuses before mint/send. Existing publishing-origin checks, incarnation/send provenance, queue ordering, idempotency and receipt semantics stay mandatory. Existing native catalogue rows/functions remain historical; select new versions explicitly, not by numeric greater-than tests. Owning maintained generation later produces new catalogue texts/pins/goldens.\n4. Add the host fence for older pinned destinations at file judge, before file-publication mint, and immediately before file-publication send/recovery using fresh policy evidence. OutsideGiven exposes only own/retained data and current SnapshotReader exposes job/key, so a narrow authenticated publication-policy reader is necessary; it must supply actual installed release/definition/child provenance plus current Rules extents, not an ambient package label. Missing proof is denied or remains unavailable according to the existing evidence contract, never granted by a cache. At old file judge, deliberate policy denial returns the existing confirmed head/present:false/tree:null evidence, retaining recorded aborted/path-invalid. Do not inject reserved/undeclared into historical outcome schemas or call deliberate denial null. A later pre-send denial uses existing truthful unsent/refused evidence and never claims certainty after an already marked send.\n5. Keep compatibility as one finite reviewed exact signed release+definition map to shelf/, checked only after genuine same-room origin/provenance. Unknown or missing pair denies; no name-based or global shelf default. The next Lending release declares shelf/ itself; planner removes the entry only after actual hosted migration. Update application docs and fold-publication section6 with an explicit supersession, preserving historical meaning. Refresh actual D1 owners/seals and note only after authored source exists. R8 integration must precede binding the implementation head, preserving all its gateway/key work.\n\nOwning witnesses, later allocated without sweeping repeats: pure prefix/reserved/effective-link controls (case aliases, nested instruction files, Git controls, dynamic authority/rules patterns, ordinary content positive, malformed/missing proof); strict codec old-byte goldens plus new signed declaration; native install denial for reserved claims; genuine new-Destination reserved/undeclared refusals with exact reasons and a committed shelf positive; old-pinned host recorded path-invalid refusal with mint/send counters zero; stale policy between judge and mint/send; absent/unknown/wrong release or definition compatibility failures; genuine Lending shelf positive and Grow no-publication install. Extend the existing whole files application-package-v2/new-version tests, extents/destination tests, application-install tests, Scope application-publication.test.ts, destination-host.test.ts and lending.test.ts as appropriate. Replay an existing pinned journal and verify exact old state/entry digests; do not change old native rules to make a test pass. Bound compiler roots from actual changed graphs, source parser/inventory, one final exact-head ordinary gate and checker review follow later. Hosted publish/readbacks and deploys remain planner-owned.\n\nRemaining uncertainties that must not be guessed. (a) Every literal directory prefix, including approved shelf/, can contain a future AGENTS.md. Therefore the prior wording reject any prefix capable of covering any reserved descendant would reject every nonempty prefix. Prefix authority must have an explicitly understood reserved subtraction/install-overlap rule; the ruling's shelf positive plus any-depth protection exposes this wording ambiguity. This plan does not silently choose broader authority or deny all prefixes. (b) Inspected historical Lending wrangler config has no exact approved signed release identity; current examples/lending/pin.ts is 0c43dd56..., while the historical runbook records 439cd20e..